---
import ReferenceFigure from "./ReferenceFigure.astro";

const root = "/studies/plasma-projector-fitting-2026-11-17";
---

<div class="references">
  <ReferenceFigure>
    <a
      slot="image"
      href={`${root}/024-doom-plasma-rifle.jpg`}
      aria-label="Enlarge DOOM Eternal plasma rifle reference"
    >
      <img
        src={`${root}/024-doom-plasma-rifle.jpg`}
        width="1920"
        height="1296"
        alt="DOOM Eternal plasma rifle: a broad slotted forebody, heavy front plate, circular side housing and exposed curved pipework"
      >
    </a>
    <h3>DOOM Eternal / A substantial working body</h3>
    <p>
      The pale slotted section occupies much of the forebody. A thick front
      plate terminates it; exposed pipes visibly connect the large rear housing
      to neighbouring parts. These relationships remain visible without a firing
      effect.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Reading:</strong>
      repeated ribs and connected machinery give heat and power a physical
      presence. Their scale in the assembly matters more here than surface
      scratches or small vents. This is an interpretation of the artwork, not a
      claim about its fictional internals.
    </p>
    <p class="credit">
      <a href="https://neilmcknight.artstation.com/projects/lxr1yO"
        >Neil McKnight’s production model and textures</a
      >, from concept art by Jon Lane. DOOM Eternal, id Software / Bethesda.
      Source image retained unaltered for this comparison.
    </p>
  </ReferenceFigure>
  <ReferenceFigure>
    <a
      slot="image"
      href={`${root}/024-halo-plasma-pistol.jpg`}
      aria-label="Enlarge Halo Infinite plasma pistol reference"
    >
      <img
        src={`${root}/024-halo-plasma-pistol.jpg`}
        width="1920"
        height="1080"
        alt="Halo Infinite plasma pistol: purple shell pieces frame a broad exposed green-lit face and a pronounced opening at the front"
      >
    </a>
    <h3>Halo Infinite / An exposed working face</h3>
    <p>
      The separated upper and lower shell pieces frame an open front. A broad
      internal face carries the green light across that opening. The luminous
      material has a substantial surface and a visible relationship to the
      surrounding shell.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Reading:</strong>
      the opening and its internal face establish an energy device. The alien
      curves belong to Halo; the transferable relationship is a clearly exposed
      working surface held within a larger assembly. This image alone cannot
      establish how the unlit weapon reads.
    </p>
    <p class="credit">
      <a href="https://mikejohnfrank86.artstation.com/projects/WmdrxN"
        >Michael Frank’s high-resolution Plasma Pistol model</a
      >
      for Halo Infinite, 343 Industries / Microsoft. Source image retained
      unaltered for this comparison.
    </p>
  </ReferenceFigure>
</div>
